From cbe5a11283eb60d89150dbfa09a30e55f8b8529e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haofeng Li <lihaofeng@kylinos.cn>
Date: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 13:39:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] smb: smbdirect: reject zero-length RDMA transfers

ksmbd accepts an SMB2 WRITE request using an RDMA channel with
RemainingBytes set to zero. smb2_write_rdma_channel() then passes a zero
buffer length to smbdirect_connection_rdma_xmit().

For a zero-length transfer, smbdirect_connection_rdma_xmit() breaks out
of descriptor accounting before adding any descriptors, leaving desc_num
and credits_needed as zero. The zero-credit wait succeeds, no RDMA
contexts are built, first_wr remains NULL, and the function can reach the
empty-list completion wait path with no work request that can signal it.

Reject zero-length RDMA WRITE requests in ksmbd and make
smbdirect_connection_rdma_xmit() reject zero-length transfers or missing
descriptors before building work requests.

Fixes: 6cc55655d0bc ("smb: smbdirect: introduce smbdirect_rw.c with server rw code")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Haofeng Li <lihaofeng@kylinos.cn>
---
 fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c | 2 +-
 fs/smb/smbdirect/rw.c   | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c b/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c
index c1c6c1a64f60..170cf10f2768 100644
--- a/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c
+++ b/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c
@@ -7307,7 +7307,7 @@ int smb2_write(struct ksmbd_work *work)
 	if (is_rdma_channel == true) {
 		unsigned int ch_offset = le16_to_cpu(req->WriteChannelInfoOffset);
 
-		if (req->Length != 0 || req->DataOffset != 0 ||
+		if (req->Length != 0 || req->DataOffset != 0 || !length ||
 		    ch_offset < offsetof(struct smb2_write_req, Buffer)) {
 			err = -EINVAL;
 			goto out;
diff --git a/fs/smb/smbdirect/rw.c b/fs/smb/smbdirect/rw.c
index 6fe38042cfb9..2d511d0c3b88 100644
--- a/fs/smb/smbdirect/rw.c
+++ b/fs/smb/smbdirect/rw.c
@@ -129,6 +129,9 @@ int smbdirect_connection_rdma_xmit(struct smbdirect_socket *sc,
 	if (buf_len > sp->max_read_write_size)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	if (!buf_len || desc_len < sizeof(*desc))
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	/* calculate needed credits */
 	credits_needed = 0;
 	desc_buf = buf;
-- 
2.55.0

